{"title":"Dense","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Dense&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p><p><br />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Topological_space\" title=\"Topological space\">topological space</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Subspace&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Subspace (page does not exist)\">subspace</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is <b>dense</b> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> if, for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e789763cfcc6a3688812b3660fda9b6d9cc80a4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x\\in X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> and any <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Open_set\" title=\"Open set\">open</a> neighborhood <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c320fd5bcd1fd49d16ec23b50163191198545b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U\\ni x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e269c8397c34fd6faebe2f3427b73595b6ba52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$U\\cap S\\neq\\varnothing$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"17\" />. For example, the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rational_number\" title=\"Rational number\">rational numbers</a> are dense in the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real numbers</a>.\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018082358\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.011 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 31/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 256/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1399/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.115      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.115      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2116:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018082358 and revision id 9696. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}